    "description": "The Alborz and Zagros are major mountain systems with different positions, structures and environmental contrasts. The Alborz separates the Caspian lowlands from Iran’s interior, while the Zagros forms a broad belt of folded and faulted terrain across western Iran. [s1][s2][s3]",
    "tags": ["Alborz", "Zagros", "Physical geography", "Plate tectonics", "Mountain ecosystems"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "ready_for_review",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
